{"d.Log is passed instead of the operation-scoped log variable that includes context fields (name, kind, method), losing diagnostic information in downstream logs and async context for legacy writes": 0.9664167165756226, "recordLegacyDuration is called when unified Storage.Create fails, but should be recordStorageDuration instead - this misattributes storage failures to legacy operations in metrics, skewing migration readiness dashboards and SLO calculations": 0.9962723255157471, "name (object name) is passed as a metric label where other methods use options.Kind for resource kind - this introduces high cardinality and breaks metric consistency across operations": 0.9818041324615479, "Inside the async legacy DeleteCollection goroutine, recordStorageDuration is called instead of recordLegacyDuration - this mislabels legacy async operation metrics": 0.9982008934020996, "Async legacy writes lack any logging on failure\u2014only metrics\u2014which breaks visibility into divergence between unified and legacy storage during rollback scenarios": 0.9511865973472595, "Unbounded goroutine spawning under high write load or slow legacy backends creates resource leak risk": 0.777725100517273, "Hardcoded 10-second timeout is not tunable across environments": 0.38619089126586914, "No backpressure or queue depth visibility exists for async operations": 0.5442665815353394, "Unit tests don't validate async behavior completes": 0.5682623386383057, "Integration tests don't verify cross-store consistency or dual-write metrics": 0.2406325340270996, "No timeout or goroutine lifecycle scenarios are tested": 0.565589189529419}